/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A storing closure is handed to a function that casts it inside a rabbit of its own.

    The hand-over is judged as though the function were cast there; a receiver that casts it somewhere
    deeper breaks that, so each function records which function parameters it does that with. (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O4). */

Bind void to visit, given (the series of series of number rows, the void function work given (the series of number)):
    Pull a rabbit.
        Define scratch as a series of number with (9).
        Cast work on (scratch).
    Done.
Done.
Define rows as a series of series of number.
Insert (a series of number with (1, 2)) into rows.
Define collected as a series of series of number.
Cast visit on (rows, a function given (the series of number row):
    Insert row into collected.
Done).
State collected.
